title: 'Missions wait mostly on the model: the tests take about a tenth of all working time, and a quarter of a build mission''s.'
pid: 8eaadf31-7921-49f5-9c46-2b05b6138cd0
body: |2-
  Measured from every session's record since 2026-11-10, timing each
  tool call from its start to its result. Time a session spent waiting
  on a mind it lent out is counted once, in that mind's own record.
  The suite is slow by setting more than by hardware: it runs the Rust
  tests one at a time, runs the integration tests one at a time, and
  one integration test waits 40 s for nothing. On four small cores it
  used under one core on average. So a bigger machine would not speed
  it much, and a smaller one would not slow it much.
  At least 20 minutes in those five days were sessions waiting for
  another session's build or tests to finish, because two suites
  cannot run at once: the integration tests edit their fixtures in place.
  What would shorten missions most is fewer or shorter model turns, which
  no machine buys.
  If you do not answer, the suite stays as it is.
contains:
